# MARLEY reaction data for charged current ve on 52Cr
# Revised 29 October 2026 by Justin Skweres
#
# Particle IDs conform to the 2017 revision of the
# Particle Data Group Monte Carlo Particle Numbering Scheme
# (see http://pdg.lbl.gov/2018/reviews/rpp2018-rev-monte-carlo-numbering.pdf)
#
# B(GT) values for levels in 52Cr from 5.0 MeV and below were taken from D. Wang and J.
# Rapaport, et al., Nucl. Phys. A 480, (1988). For energies between 5.6 MeV and 17.0 MeV,
# B(GT) values were taken from 1 MeV histogram bin vlaues in the same paper. Experimental values were multiplied
# by g_A^2 = (1.26)^2 to account for their differing definition of B(GT), which did
# not include that weak axial-vector coupling constant.
#
# The B(F) value was taken as the sum-rule value g_V^2*(N_i - Z_i) with g_V=1
#
# Particle IDs and final ion charge
0 1000240520
